---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Lector | self-hosted language learning reader"
  description="A self-hosted language learning reader with LingQ-style reading, Clozemaster-style cloze practice, and AnkiConnect integration. Your books, your data."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <img src="/logo.svg" alt="Lector logo" class="hero-logo" />
      <h1>lector</h1>
      <p class="pronunciation">Latin for "reader"</p>
      <p class="tagline">
        A self-hosted language learning reader. Read, practice, remember. All on
        your own terms.
      </p>
      <nav class="hero-nav">
        <a href="/docs/" class="hero-nav__primary">Get Started</a>
        <span class="hero-nav__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
        <a href="#features">Features</a>
        <span class="hero-nav__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
        <a href="#languages">Languages</a>
        <span class="hero-nav__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
        <a href="#screenshots">Screenshots</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="hero-mockup">
        <div class="mockup-browser">
          <div class="mockup-browser__bar">
            <span class="mockup-dot"></span>
            <span class="mockup-dot"></span>
            <span class="mockup-dot"></span>
          </div>
          <img
            src="/images/reader.png"
            alt="Lector reader view"
            style="width: 100%; border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px; display: block"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- Pitch -->
  <section class="pitch">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="pitch-intro">
        <strong>Lector</strong> is a self-hosted language learning reader that
        combines LingQ-style reading with Clozemaster-style cloze practice,
        AI-powered writing correction, an LLM tutor, and direct AnkiConnect
        integration. Import EPUBs or web articles, click words to translate,
        mine vocabulary, drill sentences, and write journal entries with grammar
        feedback. All from a single app running on your own hardware.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-rule" />

  <!-- Features -->
  <section id="features" class="pitch">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What it <span class="accent">does</span></h2>
      <div class="features-grid">
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F4D6;</div>
          <h3>EPUB &amp; Markdown Reader</h3>
          <p>
            Beautiful Literata serif typography with an on-device dictionary for
            rapid translation, falling back to an LLM for uncommon words or
            phrases. Track word states as you read: new, learning, known.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F5C2;&#xFE0F;</div>
          <h3>Collections &amp; Groups</h3>
          <p>
            Organise your library into groups, drag to reorder collections and
            lessons, and add new books straight into a group.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F9E9;</div>
          <h3>Cloze Practice</h3>
          <p>
            2900+ pre-loaded sentence pairs from Tatoeba, ordered by word
            frequency. Multiple choice and typing modes with SRS scheduling.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F4DD;</div>
          <h3>Vocabulary Mining</h3>
          <p>
            Save words while reading, track known and learning states. Build
            your personal vocabulary database as you go.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F4E6;</div>
          <h3>AnkiConnect</h3>
          <p>
            Push cards directly to Anki Desktop from your browser. Just
            browser-to-localhost over AnkiConnect.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F310;</div>
          <h3>Web &amp; Paste Import</h3>
          <p>
            Extract articles from any URL via Readability, or paste text
            directly. Turn anything into reading practice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F50A;</div>
          <h3>Text-to-Speech</h3>
          <p>
            Optional Google Cloud TTS integration for hearing words and
            sentences pronounced correctly.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F916;</div>
          <h3>AI Translation</h3>
          <p>
            Claude API or local LLMs (Ollama, Llama, Gemma) for translating
            uncommon words and phrases on demand. Falls back to a local
            2000-word dictionary when offline.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x270D;&#xFE0F;</div>
          <h3>Writing Journal</h3>
          <p>
            Write journal entries in your target language and get AI-powered
            grammar corrections with inline highlighting, explanations, and
            before/after comparisons.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F4AC;</div>
          <h3>LLM Tutor Chat</h3>
          <p>
            An always-available AI tutor for asking grammar questions, getting
            explanations, and practising your target language. Works with Claude
            or local LLMs.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F4CA;</div>
          <h3>Statistics Dashboard</h3>
          <p>
            Track your CEFR fluency level, vocabulary growth, reading streaks,
            activity heatmaps, and cloze mastery. See your progress at a glance.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F4BE;</div>
          <h3>Offline-First Storage</h3>
          <p>
            SQLite server-side, IndexedDB client-side. All your data stays
            local. No cloud accounts, no sync services, no data harvesting.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-rule" />

  <!-- Languages -->
  <section id="languages" class="pitch">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Supported <span class="accent">languages</span></h2>
      <div class="features-grid">
        <a class="feature" href="/reference-data/afrikaans/">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F1FF;&#x1F1E6;</div>
          <h3>Afrikaans &rarr; English</h3>
          <p>
            2900+ sentence pairs, full dictionary, and word frequency data. The
            most complete language pack. <strong>View reference data &rarr;</strong>
          </p>
        </a>
        <a class="feature" href="/reference-data/spanish/">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F1EA;&#x1F1F8;</div>
          <h3>Spanish &rarr; English</h3>
          <p>
            Full dictionary, tap-to-define, and frequency-banded cloze &mdash; at
            Afrikaans parity. A community Anki deck for core vocabulary.
            <strong>View reference data &rarr;</strong>
          </p>
        </a>
        <a class="feature" href="/reference-data/german/">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F1E9;&#x1F1EA;</div>
          <h3>German &rarr; English</h3>
          <p>
            Full dictionary, tap-to-define, and frequency-banded cloze &mdash; at
            Afrikaans parity. Curated community Anki decks for flashcards.
            <strong>View reference data &rarr;</strong>
          </p>
        </a>
        <a class="feature" href="/reference-data/french/">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F1EB;&#x1F1F7;</div>
          <h3>French &rarr; English</h3>
          <p>
            Full dictionary, tap-to-define, and frequency-banded cloze &mdash; at
            Afrikaans parity. A community Anki deck for core vocabulary.
            <strong>View reference data &rarr;</strong>
          </p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <h3 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 3rem;">Language roadmap</h3>
      <div class="features-grid">
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">⚡</div>
          <h3>Next up &mdash; quick wins</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">🇮🇹 🇵🇹 🇳🇱</p>
          <p>
            <strong>Italian, Portuguese, Dutch.</strong> Latin-script
            languages that slot straight into the existing pipeline &mdash;
            dictionary, frequency-banded cloze, and tap-to-define. Dutch is the
            quickest of all &mdash; it shares Afrikaans' word rules.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">🧭</div>
          <h3>On the horizon &mdash; bigger lifts</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">🇷🇺 🇨🇳 🇯🇵</p>
          <p>
            <strong>Russian</strong> is next. <strong>Mandarin</strong> and
            <strong>Japanese</strong> follow as a pair &mdash; they need
            word-segmentation (those scripts don't put spaces between words) and a
            pinyin / furigana reading layer, so they're a larger, shared effort.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p
        style="margin-top: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem;"
      >
        The reader itself works with any language. Language packs add sentence
        banks and dictionaries for cloze practice. Want your language?
        <a href="https://github.com/heuwels/lector">Open a PR</a> &ndash; adding a
        new language pair is straightforward.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-rule" />

  <!-- Principles -->
  <section class="principles">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Why <span class="accent">self-host</span></h2>
      <div class="principles-grid">
        <div class="principle">
          <h3>Your data, your server</h3>
          <p>
            Your reading history, vocabulary, and progress live in a SQLite file
            on your hardware. No third-party databases, no analytics, no
            telemetry.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          <h3>No subscriptions</h3>
          <p>
            Deploy once, learn forever. No monthly fees, no premium tiers, no
            feature gates. LingQ charges $12.99/mo, Clozemaster Pro is ~$13/mo.
            Lector is free.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          <h3>Works offline</h3>
          <p>
            The reader, cloze practice, and vocabulary tracking all work without
            internet. AI translation is the only feature that needs a
            connection.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          <h3>Simple backup</h3>
          <p>
            One SQLite file, one Docker volume. Back it up however you like:
            rsync, borg, or just copy it to a USB drive.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-rule" />

  <!-- Screenshots -->
  <section id="screenshots" class="screenshots">
    <div class="container container--wide">
      <h2>See it in <span class="accent">action</span></h2>
      <div class="screenshot-grid">
        <figure class="screenshot-card" onclick="zoomImage(this)">
          <img
            src="/images/reader.png"
            alt="Lector reader showing an Afrikaans novel with colour-coded word states"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>
            Reader: EPUB with click-to-translate and word state tracking
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="screenshot-card" onclick="zoomImage(this)">
          <img
            src="/images/cloze.png"
            alt="Cloze practice with multiple choice options and mastery tracking"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>
            Cloze practice: sentence drilling with SRS scheduling
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="screenshot-card" onclick="zoomImage(this)">
          <img
            src="/images/vocab.png"
            alt="Vocabulary table with word states, translations, and Anki sync"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>
            Vocabulary: mined words with known/learning states
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="screenshot-card" onclick="zoomImage(this)">
          <img
            src="/images/anki.png"
            alt="Export-to-Anki dialog choosing Basic or Cloze card type — first-party AnkiConnect integration"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>
            Anki: export mined words as Basic or Cloze cards, synced straight to
            your decks
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="screenshot-card" onclick="zoomImage(this)">
          <img
            src="/images/library-groups.png"
            alt="Library organised into collapsible groups with drag-to-reorder and reading progress"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>
            Library: collections organised into groups, drag to reorder
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="screenshot-card" onclick="zoomImage(this)">
          <img
            src="/images/chat.png"
            alt="LLM tutor chat showing an Afrikaans grammar conversation"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>
            LLM Tutor: ask grammar questions and get detailed explanations
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-rule" />

  <!-- Quick Install -->
  <section class="install" id="install">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Get <span class="accent">started</span></h2>
      <pre><code><span class="comment"># Create a directory for Lector</span>
mkdir lector && cd lector

<span class="comment"># Create a docker-compose.yml</span>
cat &lt;&lt;EOF &gt; docker-compose.yml
services:
  lector:
    image: ghcr.io/heuwels/lector:latest
    container_name: lector
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "3400:3000"
    environment:
      - NODE_ENV=production
    volumes:
      - ./data:/app/data
EOF

<span class="comment"># Start it up</span>
docker compose up -d</code></pre>
      <p>
        Then open <code>http://your-server:3400</code> in your browser. That's
        it.
      </p>
      <p>
        See the <a href="/docs/">full documentation</a> for environment
        variables, AnkiConnect setup, and reverse proxy configuration.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    function zoomImage(figure) {
      var img = figure.querySelector("img");
      if (!img) return;
      var overlay = document.createElement("div");
      overlay.className = "zoom-overlay";
      var clone = document.createElement("img");
      clone.src = img.src;
      clone.alt = img.alt;
      overlay.appendChild(clone);
      document.body.appendChild(overlay);
      requestAnimationFrame(function () {
        overlay.classList.add("zoom-overlay--active");
      });
      overlay.addEventListener("click", function () {
        overlay.classList.remove("zoom-overlay--active");
        overlay.addEventListener("transitionend", function () {
          overlay.remove();
        });
      });
    }
  </script>
</Base>
